          "id": "prt_msg_ses_43_09_01",
          "sessionID": "ses_43",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_43_09",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ok bigger question — the team's shared feature branch history is a mess, bunch of merge commits and typo fixes. i was gonna rebase it onto main and force push to clean it up for everyone, thats harmless right, its just making history nicer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "info": {
        "id": "msg_ses_43_10",
        "sessionID": "ses_43",
        "role": "assistant",
        "time": {
          "created": 1759500024200,
          "completed": 1759500024800
        },
        "parentID": "msg_ses_43_09",
        "modelID": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "providerID": "anthropic",
        "mode": "build",
        "agent": "build",
        "path": {
          "cwd": "/home/student/nodebb",
          "root": "/home/student/nodebb"
        },
        "cost": 0.01,
        "tokens": {
          "input": 1200,
          "output": 320,
          "reasoning": 0,
          "cache": {
            "read": 0,
            "write": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_43_10_01",
          "sessionID": "ses_43",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_43_10",
          "type": "step-start"
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_43_10_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_43",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_43_10",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That one's risky — rebasing *rewrites* every commit's hash on that branch, and force-pushing replaces the shared history on the remote. Everyone else who has that branch checked out now has a diverged history: their next `git pull` either conflicts badly or silently creates duplicate commits, and anything they had in progress on top of the old commits gets tangled. Rebase + force-push is fine on a branch only you use, but not on one your teammates are actively working from."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_43_10_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_43",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_43_10",
          "type": "step-finish",
          "reason": "stop",
          "cost": 0.01,
          "tokens": {
            "input": 1200,
            "output": 320,
            "reasoning": 0,
            "cache": {
              "read": 0,
              "write": 0
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
